59
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Version generator

60
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Through the measurement point or grass map,

61
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:05,000
you can quickly and easily create a costume in Marvelous Designer.

62
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Click on the 2D version menu,

63
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,000
then select the version generator.

64
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Next, please select the costume type.

65
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Currently, it only supports the production of T-shirts,

66
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
and will add more options later.

67
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
Then,

68
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,000
according to the style you need to choose,

69
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
the T-shirt style is divided by the sleeve type.

70
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Below, you will see the basic measurement data of the costume.

71
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
As for how to check and adjust your measurement data,

72
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
you have three different options.

73
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:37,000
The regular option will provide you with a complete list of the common measurement points of the costume.

74
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:41,000
The simple option will provide you with the most common measurement points,

75
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,000
to simplify the editing process.

76
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:48,000
The user's self-definition option allows you to customize your own measurement list,

77
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
and according to the required self-definition measurement data.

78
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
You can click on the eye icon

79
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
to select which costume versions to be created.

80
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:07,000
You can switch the version to symmetrical or left-right symmetrical.

81
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
The measurement options for all measurement options

82
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
can be used to display all measurement data for each version.

83
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Click on the Detailed Information button.

84
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
You can switch to the list of all measurement information.

85
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
According to the measurement data that needs to be selected and displayed.

86
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
After the setting is complete,

87
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:35,000
click on the button to change the application.

88
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Enter your version measurement value.

89
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:45,000
You can click on the reset button next to each measurement data

90
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
to restore it to its original value.

91
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Some measurement items will contain a total length option

92
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
used to enter the total dimension of the front and back pieces.

93
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Some measurement items also contain a pull-down option

94
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:00,000
used to select the measurement location applied to the measurement data.

95
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:05,000
You can click to display all measurement icons

96
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:09,000
to view all non-actual measurement items in each part.

97
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Click on the Create button to create costumes in the 2D and 3D windows.

98
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:21,000
The AI version generator is available.

99
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:27,000
Using the data generated by the Marvelous Designer

100
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,000
will automatically generate measurement data.

101
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
To create a draft version for you,

102
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,000
click on the AI version generator button in the upper right corner of the version generator.

103
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
By entering the keyword to generate a picture

104
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
or directly upload a picture to generate the result,

105
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
select the type of costume,

106
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
and input your draft inspiration.

107
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Please make sure to add as many descriptive words as possible.

108
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,000
If you want to emphasize some content, please put it in the brackets.

109
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Currently only T-shape can be selected,

110
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
and more other styles will be introduced later.

111
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:04,000
A small tip, please try to provide words that describe accurately,

112
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:08,000
and not long sentences, to produce more effective results.

113
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Clicking on the key word suggestion will display the power key word,

114
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
which will help you generate keywords.

115
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Even if you use the same keyword, the AI picture will be re-created every time.

116
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Therefore, clicking on the key word button

117
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
can keep the existing results as long as possible

118
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
while updating the key word.

119
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
According to the addition or change of the key word,

120
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
the result may be different from the existing result.

121
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Clicking on the random generate button

122
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,000
will randomly add the power key word to the text prompt.

123
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Click on the key word button,

124
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
click on the generate button to create a picture.

125
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Click on the delete button to delete all input contents

126
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
and start creating again.

127
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Click on the upload button to upload a reference image that meets the following guidelines.

128
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Use the white background, black lines of the clothing draft

129
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,000
to ensure high-quality AI versions are generated.

130
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Ensure that there are only clothing drafts in the image.

131
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:22,000
This process can be repeated until you get the desired result.

132
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,000
You can find the image history record generated by you on the right side of the window.

133
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Self-designed model software simulation

134
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Now software model simulation can be used for self-designed virtual models,

135
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:37,000
including simple non-human shapes or human virtual models without Google.

136
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
Software simulation can be used for OBJ and FBX virtual models.

137
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Now add an OBJ or FBX virtual model.

138
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Here we add an OBJ file,

139
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
then confirm the imported virtual model.

140
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Please note that the imported virtual model

141
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
cannot have a hole or a self-interference problem.

142
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Go to the virtual model rendering type in the 3D window.

143
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:05,000
Select semi-transparent surface or display frame to preview and check for potential problems.

144
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Insert clothing that matches the size of the virtual model,

145
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,000
or create a set of clothing for the virtual model.

146
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Now we have added a set of clothing.

147
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Open the software model simulation option.

148
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Select the virtual model and then go to the attribute editor.

149
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
You can select software model simulation under the surface.

150
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Please remember to select CPU simulation and then open the simulation.

151
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
In this example,

152
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:40,000
we will adjust the software model strength to 6500.

153
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Then speed up to see the final result.

154
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
In addition,

155
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,000
you can also apply software model simulation to simple structural objects.

156
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
In this example,

157
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
we are using a very simple object.

158
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:56,000
You can find it in the drawing library, virtual model, and fill-in model.

159
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Please confirm again that your model has no hole or self-interference problem.

160
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,000
You can go to the 3D window and select semi-transparent surface.

161
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
You can also choose to open the frame display.

162
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:09,000
To see the cloth line more clearly and whether there is a gap.

163
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Now we add fabric outside of this model.

164
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Create a rectangular plate.

165
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Put it on the virtual model.

166
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Open the simulation and let it hang on the model.

167
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Now we use the sewing tool to sew the two ends of this fabric together.

168
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,000
In this example,

169
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
we will reduce the particle diameter to 10,

170
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,000
then harden the plate.

171
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Make the simulation more stable,

172
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:38,000
the effect is more obvious.

173
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Select the model,

174
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,000
then open the software model simulation in the attribute editor.

175
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,000
Also remember to switch to CPU simulation,

176
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
then open the simulation.

177
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Reduce the strength of the software model to 5000.

178
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:55,000
We will see the effect of the model under pressure.

179
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Failure elimination.

180
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
If your virtual model has a gap or hole,

181
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
an error window will pop up.

182
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
In this example,

183
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:06,000
this model has a hole and insertion problem at the same time.

184
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
According to the conventional operation steps,

185
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
this model will be converted into a virtual model.

186
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,000
After loading,

187
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,000
we create a template to affect this model.

188
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Then open the simulation,

189
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,000
simulate the fabric on the model.

190
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,000
If you try to use the software simulation function,

191
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
you will see the error prompt

192
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
and point out the current file problem.

193
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
We already know that

194
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:33,000
this file has two errors at the same time,

195
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,000
insertion and hole.

196
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
The prompt will also prompt the same error.

197
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
If you click OK,

198
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
it will turn off the spring,

199
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,000
cancel the activation of the software model simulation.

200
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:44,000
Therefore,

201
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,000
we recommend you again

202
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
to open the semi-transparent display

203
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
or open the display frame

204
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
